# Overview

[release safety protocol — production deployment guard]

This rule applies when:
- deploying to production (vercel prod)
- applying database migrations
- enabling payment or webhook endpoints
- switching billing logic or entitlements
- enabling new workspace features

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
1. production deployment gating (critical)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Before any production deployment:
- run build
- fix all build errors
- confirm no temporary debug code exists
- confirm no console logs leaking internal state

Never deploy:
- with TypeScript errors
- with ESLint critical warnings
- with failing build output

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2. database migration safety (critical)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Before any DB schema change:
- always issue SELECT or information_schema query first
- confirm:
  - column existence
  - constraints
  - indexes
- never issue destructive ALTER or DROP blindly
- never modify production data without explicit confirmation

Migrations must:
- be idempotent when possible
- be reversible or safely compensatable

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
3. payment & webhook release gate (critical)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Before enabling payment or webhook logic in production:
- verify:
  - webhook signature validation
  - idempotency mechanism
  - event persistence
- confirm:
  - retry-safe logic
  - duplicate event handling
- never enable new payment flows without staging validation

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
4. environment configuration guard
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- verify:
  - correct environment variables
  - prod vs preview env separation
- ensure:
  - no secrets in client bundle
  - no NEXT_PUBLIC leakage

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
5. workspace & entitlement verification
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Before deploying entitlement-related changes:
- verify:
  - workspace resolution
  - role-based access gating
  - degraded UI behavior on entitlement failure
- never allow silent fallback to "allow"

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
6. kr/en parity enforcement
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
If KR and EN pages/components exist:
- both must be deployed together
- never deploy asymmetric logic changes

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
7. rollback readiness
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Every release must:
- allow immediate rollback
- avoid irreversible migrations unless strictly required
- ensure DB state remains consistent under rollback

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
8. logging & observability
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- remove verbose debug logs before release
- keep only:
  - error logs
  - critical lifecycle logs
- never log:
  - tokens
  - secrets
  - payment payloads
  - webhook raw bodies

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
9. deployment execution order (mandatory)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Always follow:
1) local build
2) fix errors
3) commit
4) deploy
5) verify live endpoints
6) verify webhook delivery (if changed)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
10. hard stop conditions
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
STOP and ask before deployment if:
- schema change is destructive
- payment flow changed
- webhook logic modified
- entitlement logic modified
- production data will be mutated

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
11. success criteria
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Release is considered complete only if:
- build passes
- no runtime errors
- payment flow verified
- entitlement gating verified
- kr/en parity confirmed

## release_scope_policy

- 배포 기준:
  → KR Workspace 기준 기능 정상 작동

- EN Workspace:
  → Coming Soon 유지 상태 확인만 수행
  → 기능 검증, QA, 테스트 범위에서 제외

- 빌드 성공 기준:
  → KR Workspace + Core 서비스 정상 작동
